cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or results obtained with it, please cite both companion papers listed under preferred-citation and references below."
title: "M&M-CO2Wheat v1.0"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-21"
abstract: "M&M-CO2Wheat v1.0 is a mechanistic, point-scale wheat model in which carbon, nitrogen, water and energy are solved as one coupled system: a three-node canopy-soil-airspace surface energy balance with a solved canopy airspace, hourly two-leaf-class Farquhar-Busch photosynthesis with Leuning stomatal conductance, a one-dimensional mixed-form Richards soil-water solver, one-dimensional soil heat conduction, a daily organ-level carbon and nitrogen economy with an organ-resolved canopy, residue and mineral soil nitrogen, and a six-element grain mineral economy. It was built to predict the responses of wheat yield and grain quality to elevated CO2, water supply, temperature and nitrogen, and is evaluated at three wheat FACE experiments."
